  "note": "Triennial election of the Dromore Urban Council, polled Friday 15 January 1932. Only the seven surviving members of the old Council were nominated and were declared re-elected unopposed; two co-options were needed to bring the Council up to nine (Dromore Leader, 9 January 1932, p. 3). F. R. Hamilton and James Dickson had died since the last election and no co-options had been made, so the term finished with seven members instead of nine. Returned unopposed."
